evidence.en:
socket.on("message", (msg) => {
  setMessages((prev) => [...prev, msg]);
  // worked in React 17: DOM already had the new <li> here
  listRef.current.lastChild.scrollIntoView();
});

In React 17, updates outside React event handlers were flushed synchronously per call, so the DOM was committed before scrollIntoView ran. React 18 applies automatic ___b1___ to all contexts, so the commit now happens after the whole callback — the scroll reads the old DOM. The targeted fix is wrapping the state update in ___b2___ so the commit is forced before the scroll, accepting the cost of a synchronous ___b3___ on the main thread.

